  "description": "FOZFOS crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H70 Dy4 N18 O26,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.660-3.985 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.30-110.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H70Dy4N18O26·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
